#{[17592186375296 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375296 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375296 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1ff7b33-78b9-5494-b1f6-21fedac20ac0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375297 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375297 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375297 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1dc8f458-65bc-5c8d-90ae-6ef401a3ebd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375298 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375298 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375298 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "67431a46-73ba-543b-b5f2-c0345c743beb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375299 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375299 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375299 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "52a7d1c6-e780-567b-a541-1a25d2b17a20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72318" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f42f9772-6905-5ddc-bad3-1a0fe74e1330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375314 #edb/ref 1074 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/bf/bf2098a7fcdecce8405dadf6f9cd2c78da19d1c0a7ae2c9c9e95a897a64ef9d9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186375320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375315 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7caf983d-6da5-5ae9-b908-c6e8bf00bc8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375316 #edb/ref 1080 "images/7c/7c634f90a086b28d8d8c2f5cb898a149a885803851dedcf94ed6e8782ad1e25d.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375316 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375316 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dea59bf2-3509-5e23-bc45-8a6f00f8f763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375317 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the listed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375317 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375317 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cfddd069-ef87-5e55-83af-2dcabd0224f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375318 #edb/ref 1080 "images/06/062003a83f4afa0cadd68eee54dc0379e469041f3fd0b2371acf5428d8709306.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375318 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375318 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e0121ce2-27fc-58d8-947a-5788ad384bcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375319 #edb/ref 1080 "images/ef/ef9d0a612a093852fd9f60fb20c86b946c178f9e2a9877ef7c16f89f98e324f6.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375319 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375319 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d74f904-81a5-542a-b32a-e0709ccd1fed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375320 #edb/ref 1080 "images/67/677097b290404e318a097ee79fba82a2f3217ce2762df983229b75ef3d493f13.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375320 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375320 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3631542a-0a0a-5e75-9d2a-b39d672ba7dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/88/8861ad010cbd19d897ace4c8da2fdaeca25e9d2319ab95d3b338e6db49aa21ae.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8dcd36b-62ff-51dd-911e-391155781896" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375328 #edb/ref 1074 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=y+1\\,⟹\\,y=x-1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=3.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/15/15f9c5d526747b80766a8a3250fa2e705d5d7d9561c52e08492b7a18f1483eb6.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $y=x-1.$ So, we have $\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186435870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186375329 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 175921864358